{
  "case_id": "2011-10-694",
  "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 1,
        "start": 1
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 11:07 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mark C. Fleming",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In Hernandez-Casillas, the Attorney General confirmed that a lawful permanent resident subject to deportation, quote, \"must have the same opportunity to seek discretionary relief as an alien who has temporarily left this country and upon reentry been subject to exclusion.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "How do you explain -- I mean, I think that is a principal point, whether Blake and Brieva changed the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "NIJC",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0000-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 11,
        "start": 11
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The NIJC amicus brief, which is before the Court in this case, identifies a couple of situations, including the case of Mr. Ronald Bennett, who was advised by his lawyer that when he pled guilty, it would not be a problem for him for his immigration status because he could seek 212(c) protection."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 20,
        "start": 20
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: What about the comparability of the crime involved in St. Cyr? That was a drug offense. Does the inadmissibility criterion -- does that accord with the one for deportation?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLEMING: Well, the board in Blake concluded that that was -- that the linguistic comparison worked there so that it did not have to find itself at odds with this Court's decision in St. Cyr."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Mr. Fleming, the Government says that it has an interest in treating people in deportation proceedings less favorably, if you will, than people in exclusion proceedings. Do you dispute that broad premise that the government could develop a system which treated those two groups differently?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. FLEMING: That is not the way that the agency has ever treated permanent resident aliens. In fact, if that is the Government's position, that is clearly a change in the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Do you have evidence to the contrary?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: But, Mr. Gannon, suppose this: Suppose that on the exclusion side, you have this category of crimes of moral turpitude, and suppose on the deportation side, which I think is right, you have a category called crimes of violence, and you also have a category called crimes of moral turpitude. There's a time limit on that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "One is that there's no factual basis in the administrative record to -- to talk about this 1987 trip to the Philippines."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The chief examples are the ones that the board gives in the Brieva-Perez opinion, which are simple assault, which has -"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Neither is non-residential burglary which involves force against -- against property, which would therefore satisfy the definition."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In the Ninth Circuit, burglary of a residential dwelling that's occupied is not a crime involving moral turpitude."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0004",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "they all -- almost all involve two categories of offenses, drug trafficking or controlled substance offenses and crimes involving moral turpitude, things that were actually charged under the ground of deportation for crimes involving moral turpitude."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I keep going back to my question. There's only one category now, aggravated violent felony. That's the only category you're looking at. It doesn't matter, in your judgment. That -- that is your test."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Mr. Gannon, in your brief, I thought you'd conceded that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 56,
        "start": 56
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I thought it was telling, Justice Breyer, in reaction to your question which -- which was seeking an explanation of how this scheme is reasonable, the answer that counsel for the Government gave was that the BIA has been consistent with firearms and visa fraud cases, but there was no explanation as to how the Blake rule as it is now drawn is in any way a reasonable application of the law."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And even if it's not total, that is not the end of our argument because the board itself has said you, don't need a perfect match; you just need substantial overlap. And the overlap is at the very least substantial, if not complete."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Gannon",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0003-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 57,
        "start": 57
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The interest that Mr. Gannon asserted at one point about getting immigrants to put themselves into exclusion proceedings -- this is a very important point. The agency has never suggested that that is the way that it runs the railroad. On the contrary, it has expressly said the opposite."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.8,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0003-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Justice Sotomayor, your question about how many people are involved here, it is difficult to identify specific numbers because very often these cases are decided at the immigration judge level that are not reported."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2011-10-694",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "f150bfc834f20e069a8925396525dc7800b57eac221cd8d60e9b3f04f71b73a7",
      "evidence_id": "ev-f150bfc834f2-0003-0005",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted."
    },
    {
